# SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-or-later
#
# What clang-tidy looks for in JPEG-Unround's own C and C++ (c/, cpp/, tests/).
# ci/tidy.sh runs it over every file that a build compiles, and the lint job of
# every push runs that. Every check named here is an error, as every compiler
# warning is: the code is clean of them, and anything new is either a fault to fix
# or a decision to write down where it is made, with a NOLINT and the reason.
#
# The checks are the ones that find faults, or that lead to code which holds up
# better; the ones that only say how code should look are left out, since
# .clang-format says that. The list follows ADLplug-Next's. What is left out, and
# why:
#
#   bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters would have every function of two
#     integers take a type of its own for each.
#   bugprone-signed-bitwise sees the integral promotion of every uint8_t rather
#     than a signedness that could go wrong; the undefined behaviour sanitizer
#     finds the shifts that really can.
#   clang-analyzer-security.insecureAPI.DeprecatedOrUnsafeBufferHandling asks for
#     memcpy_s and its kin, which are Microsoft's and not in the C or C++ this
#     project is written in.
#   misc-include-cleaner wants every name's own header included, where a C header
#     like jpeglib.h brings its types with it by design.
#   misc-non-private-member-variables-in-classes is about classes with
#     invariants; this project's structs of plain data have none to protect.
#   modernize-redundant-void-arg would take the void out of f(void), which is the
#     one place it must not be taken out of: the void says what a function takes.
#     This project checks the other way round (ci/void-params.py): a parameter
#     list of nothing, written (), is an error there.
#
# Several of the checks here are not about faults but about saying what the code
# means: readability-implicit-bool-conversion has a pointer compared with nullptr
# and a number with 0; misc-const-correctness has a local that is never written
# say const; cppcoreguidelines-init-variables has a local hold a value from the
# line it is declared on; modernize-use-designated-initializers has the field
# named where a value goes into a struct; modernize-use-nodiscard has a function
# that answers a question say that the answer is the point of calling it.
Checks: >
  -*,
  bugprone-*,
  -bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters,
  -bugprone-signed-bitwise,
  clang-analyzer-*,
  -clang-analyzer-security.insecureAPI.DeprecatedOrUnsafeBufferHandling,
  concurrency-*,
  cppcoreguidelines-init-variables,
  cppcoreguidelines-narrowing-conversions,
  cppcoreguidelines-pro-type-cstyle-cast,
  cppcoreguidelines-pro-type-member-init,
  cppcoreguidelines-pro-type-reinterpret-cast,
  cppcoreguidelines-pro-type-static-cast-downcast,
  cppcoreguidelines-pro-type-union-access,
  cppcoreguidelines-slicing,
  cppcoreguidelines-virtual-class-destructor,
  google-explicit-constructor,
  misc-*,
  -misc-include-cleaner,
  -misc-non-private-member-variables-in-classes,
  modernize-deprecated-headers,
  modernize-use-designated-initializers,
  modernize-use-emplace,
  modernize-use-nodiscard,
  modernize-use-nullptr,
  modernize-use-equals-default,
  modernize-use-equals-delete,
  modernize-use-override,
  modernize-use-starts-ends-with,
  performance-*,
  -performance-enum-size,
  readability-implicit-bool-conversion,
  readability-misleading-indentation,
  readability-named-parameter,
  readability-non-const-parameter,
  readability-qualified-auto,
  readability-redundant-declaration,
  readability-static-accessed-through-instance

# Only this project's own code is reported in; ci/tidy.sh gives the same
# directories anchored at the root of the checkout, so that libjpeg-turbo's
# installed headers in the build directory are left out wherever it sits.
HeaderFilterRegex: '/(c|cpp|tests)/'
WarningsAsErrors: '*'
FormatStyle: none
